meta {
  name: POST valid quantity — 201 Created
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/odata/v4/orders/Orders
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "customerId": "CUST-001",
    "quantity": 25,
    "region": "EMEA"
  }
}

docs {
  ## req.reject demo — the contrast case

  Same handler, a positive quantity this time.

  req.data.quantity <= 0 is false, so req.reject never fires — the handler
  falls through and CAP writes the record normally.

  Expected: 201 Created, with a generated ID in the response.

  Run this right after the negative-quantity request to show the same
  endpoint, same handler, two completely different outcomes depending on
  one condition.
}
